### Assignment 11 test requests (VS Code "REST Client" extension, or Postman)

### All books with stock (and, after Q7, format / pages)
GET http://localhost:3000/books

### Q7 - only the ebooks (filter on a JSON field)
GET http://localhost:3000/books?format=ebook

### Q5 - customers with their order count (stored function)
GET http://localhost:3000/customers

### Customer 2's orders
GET http://localhost:3000/customers/2/orders

### Q5 - place an order through the procedure (customer 2 buys 2 copies of book 3)
POST http://localhost:3000/customers/2/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "book_id": 3, "quantity": 2 }

### Q5 - not enough stock (book 5 has only 4 copies) -> the trigger SIGNALs -> expect 409
POST http://localhost:3000/customers/2/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "book_id": 5, "quantity": 5 }

### Q5 - invalid quantity -> expect 400
POST http://localhost:3000/customers/2/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "book_id": 1, "quantity": -2 }

### Q5 - cancel an order (replace 9 with a real order id from GET /customers/2/orders)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/customers/2/orders/9

### Q5 - cancel an order that doesn't exist -> expect 404
DELETE http://localhost:3000/customers/2/orders/9999
